  <div class="lang-en">
  <div class="mis-page">
    <div class="mis-puntos"></div>

    <section class="mis-hero"><div class="mis-env">
      <div>
        <div class="mis-kick"><s></s><span>About &middot; 13+ years</span></div>
        <h1>A polymath, drawn to <em>complex problems</em></h1>
        <p class="mis-lead">Contador Privado Incorporado, tax advisor and Master in Strategic Business Management. Most days find me between data, evidence and territorial intelligence.</p>
        <div class="mis-acciones">
          <a class="mis-btn" href="#logros">Selected achievements</a>
          <a class="mis-btn mis-fantasma" href="/files/emmanuel-gutierrez-profile-en.pdf" target="_blank">Download profile</a>
          <a class="mis-btn mis-fantasma" href="/contacto">Contact</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mis-lienzo">
        <div class="mis-retrato" style="max-width: 330px; margin-left: auto;"><i class="mis-pt"></i>
          <img src="/img/profile-portrait.jpg" alt="Emmanuel Gutiérrez Pizarro" loading="lazy" />
          <span class="mis-et">EMMANUEL GUTIÉRREZ PIZARRO<br />COSTA RICA &middot; ACTIVE</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="mis-blq mis-panel"><div class="mis-env">
      <div class="mis-kick">Profile</div>
      <div class="mis-perfil">
        <div>
          <div class="mis-forma" style="grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);">
            <div class="mis-it"><h4>Languages</h4><span>Spanish and English</span></div>
            <div class="mis-it"><h4>Base</h4><span>Costa Rica</span></div>
            <div class="mis-it"><h4>Reach</h4><span>Costa Rica and Central America</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="mis-decir">I am drawn to complex problems and the systems that produce them, and I learn out loud by teaching as I go.</p>
          <p>My practice centers on innovation, data science, impact evaluation and territorial intelligence, with a growing focus on applied AI for social and collective good, data sovereignty, and education. Every project is a chance to build tools that stay in the territory.</p>
          <p>My next chapter is grounded in systems thinking and complex systems: reading territories as adaptive systems with feedback loops, leverage points and emergent dynamics. This is the lens that increasingly shapes how I design tools, read evidence and frame decisions.</p>
          <p>I coordinate the Nosara Community Census 2024, the first district-level census in Costa Rica, and I lead the Alliance for Community Development (ADC) in Nosara. I am also the author of the Nosara District Territorial Fiscal Balance, the country's first subnational fiscal study, and the research lead on the Nosara 3D Digital Twin.</p>
          <p>JP Asesores, my professional practice in Costa Rica, is the vehicle through which most of this work flows, alongside My Intelligent System, where I install intelligent systems for businesses and organizations. My experience spans applied research, partnerships with universities, international cooperation, foundations and private philanthropy throughout Central America.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

